# Banter in The Drowned Crossroads (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is drowned_crossroads): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ dc_trail1_01_rook_lucan
if name:rook_coldwake and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:dc_trail1 and not flag.vander_met
interject name:rook_coldwake: Poor drainage on this hummock, Lucan. And someone left a withered hand by the reeds without a burial.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: One mark off the quarry, if you please, for leaving its extremities in the mud.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Your Barnaby's crowding my boots again, shaking like a loose headstone.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: That yip is a grave omen of marsh predators, I assure you. Sit, Barnaby. Stay by the light.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Mind the black mud, lad. It goes down deep.
endif
-> END

~ dc_trail3_02_silas_tobin
if name:silas_vane and name:tobin_hayward and at:dc_trail3 and not flag.dc_ghoul_done
interject name:silas_vane: Smashed strongbox cart, Tobin. Somebody folded hard when the dead called the bet.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Leave it. This green fog tastes of sour marrow and split iron. Even my stitching won't hold your lungs.
interject name:silas_vane: Lucky I don't keep lungs, friend. But those reeds aren't moving with the wind.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Nothing grows right where armed men rot under a banner. Just bad seed and wet bone.
interject name:silas_vane: Then keep walking, before the fog decides we owe on the old tab.
endif
-> END

~ dc_murkwater_03_delphine_cordelia
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:cordelia_skein and at:dc_murkwater and not flag.grinning_sinner_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: A whole town on stilts, Cordelia, like a cheap matinee set. One slip and my hem's ruined for the season.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Delightfully precarious. And Mama Pelletier's pickled specimens suggest a fascinating local brine.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your Foolishness just rhymed coffin boat with petticoat. I'm ready to drop him in a crab trap.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Check the odds on the fight pit board before you bet. The crowd's death rate is very high.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Cheap seats always want blood on the sawdust, darling. Oldest billing in the business.
endif
-> END

~ dc_fort_04_rook_cordelia
if name:rook_coldwake and name:cordelia_skein and at:dc_fort and not flag.screams_done
interject name:rook_coldwake: Bedrolls in the yard and no fire clearance, Cordelia. And that throne sofa's cobbled from three evictions.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Bad stitching on the sofa, yes. But fear's put every pulse in this yard up forty per cent.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Leave their pulses out of it. They've had a rough night. Someone even left a child's toy boat.
interject name:cordelia_skein: And a banner used as a rug, stained with mud and a little arterial spray. Unhygienic.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Unruly lot, lounging in cushioned chairs while the drainage fails outside. Let's finish and go.
endif
-> END

~ dc_shack_05_delphine_tobin
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:tobin_hayward and at:dc_shack_approach and flag.shack_met and not flag.grinning_sinner_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Neon bottles on the shelf, three coppers a tag. The house is practically giving the props away.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Hands off the shelves, Delphine. The weave on these idols is stitched against the grain.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: This woven doll has hands exactly the size of mine, Tobin. Tell me you didn't make it.
interject name:tobin_hayward: I don't work in marsh reed, girl. And the dark down that stair smells of old hexing.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: He's stopped laughing over my shoulder, Tobin. Not one pun. Let's go.
endif
-> END

~ dc_lagoon_06_tobin_lucan
if name:tobin_hayward and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:dc_lagoon and not flag.grinning_sinner_slain
interject name:tobin_hayward: Magenta smoke and water that tastes of drowned rust. That's no boat, Lucan. It's a wreck wearing paint.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: A fascinating glamour on the quarry. Even Barnaby has flattened his ears at that gangplank.
interject name:tobin_hayward: My mice won't poke their noses out. Something steel is glowing under the water.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: An ambush snare dressed in faded letters. Three out of ten for subtlety.
interject name:tobin_hayward: I don't trust a plank that only looks whole from one side. Keep your lantern low.
endif
-> END

~ dc_boat_promenade_07_silas_delphine
if name:silas_vane and name:delphine_ravelle and at:dc_boat_promenade and not flag.grinning_sinner_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Soulfire, jazz, and a hundred glassy-eyed marks. This whole deck's a rigged shoe, Delphine.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: I know a papier-mache headliner when I walk on one. A paddle wheel that never turns. Overdone.
interject name:silas_vane: That bellhop hasn't blinked since we came aboard. The house doesn't let winners walk off this boat.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Fine clothes, and not a soul inside them awake enough to clap. A stage full of puppets.
interject name:silas_vane: Then keep your hands out of your pockets and don't call the tune.
endif
-> END

~ dc_lagoon_08_cordelia_tobin
if name:cordelia_skein and name:tobin_hayward and at:dc_lagoon and flag.grinning_sinner_slain
interject name:cordelia_skein: How quickly the magenta smoke clears once the source is cut out. The lagoon's gone flat and still.
interject name:tobin_hayward: The rot hasn't left, Cordelia. It's only gone quiet. Look, it's just a wreck with faded letters now.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Something steel still glows down there, cooling fast. Pity. I wanted a sample of that vapour.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Leave it in the silt. We don't need swamp humours corked in your waistcoat.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Come along, Tobin, before the mosquitoes discover you've no blood to drink.
endif
-> END
